              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for a rush, then the Marathi for a scramble."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: अनुकूल",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अनुकूल — anukūl — \"favourable\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हवामान अनुकूल असेल तर आम्ही उद्या निघू. havāmān anukūl asel tar āmhī udyā nighū. If the weather is favourable we will set out tomorrow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अनुकूल (anukūl) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit anukūla, \"following the bank or slope\" (Monier-Williams), so going with the stream."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
